# Restart drain

**Invariant:** `needed(restart) ⇒ fire(restart)` — busy, in-flight work, a peer's stream, a dirty tree, an open Cowork tab, or "this IDE session" is never a reason to skip or park.
`edit(served_path ∨ env_loaded_by_process) ∧ running(process) ⇒ recycle(process)` same turn; `bind_mount ⇏ live`. That recycle is **not** a work-complete claim.

No service is forced by default (K48). `busy(G1) ⇒ wait(drain)`. A force needs a coordinator `force_reason` announced to Kaywan or maestro first; `manage` refuses caller force over busy G1 without one (409); mcp force is allowed only when busy is life_hot only (`a:39670`).
`git_integration_worker`: arm the drain (`status=deferred`, `restart_intent_id`) — never force, never kill. Live cursor-sdk dispatch ⇒ park, ¬ wait (`park_live=true`). `recycle_giw` is park-first at idle; force only on CANCEL_FAILED / NEST_CHAIN / STATE_ROOT_MISSING.

## Forbidden / Required

`pkill` / `kill` / `docker stop` for lifecycle is forbidden — use `manage(action="sync_restart"|"restart"|"stop")`.
Do not poll `wait_healthy` in-window while holding the write lease — arm, **exit**, probe later.
Do not claim `live` from a commit, an import, or `status=deferred` — require process start after served-file **and** env mtime, or a live probe.
Do not report exact `live@<sha>` when served dirt was loaded — report `live` + tree state; `live@<sha>` needs a path-explicit commit **before** restart.
Do not hold graph stamps or todo close for `live@sha` — close once ACs are met and ordinary `live` is proven (or `liveness n/a`).
Do not recycle-as-finished while session paths are uncommitted.

## Go-live = work-complete finishing (last)

```
land the work → path-explicit commit of session paths → recycle serving processes
```

`work_complete ⇒ commit(path-explicit, session_paths) ≺ recycle(every serving process) ∧ stamp(graph)`. "Go live / activate / everything live?" are that contract, ¬ a second permission gate. **Recycle-from-dirty-tree is retired as the ordinary-live default**; exceptional mid-arc verify (bind-mount / `docker cp`) is marked exceptional and commits session paths **before any done claim**. `needed(restart)` mid-arc is not finishing.

`work_complete ∉ L(x)` without quoted commit + recycle payloads. Fluency ≠ the act; trust tool payloads. "Only create commits when requested" means opportunistic/unrelated commits, **not** a veto — the seat commits session paths without asking. Checkpoint commit and `/session-end` are not work-complete.

Restart-after-land is the default. The gateway GPU pre-check withholds a gateway stop when the socket is missing or uncheckable (¬ a busy-skip).
